  The reel_script says the theft happened 'நேற்று முன்தினம் இரவு' and the article says 'நேற்று முன்தினம் இரவு' — consistent, but the caption also says 'சிவராஜ் அளித்த புகாரில்' while the article says the complaint was filed by Sivaraj; no issue there. However, the slides_spec line 'கண்வலி கிழங்கு ஒரு கிலோ விதை ரூ.4,000 வரை விற்பனை' is ungrammatical/unclear and mixes the seed-price fact into the police-investigation slide, making two different facts mixed into one sentence.
  The reel_script omits the article's fact that the stolen tubers were ready for harvest only in passing—this is present, so not missing; however the reel_script and caption state 'இதையடுத்து அவர் புகார் அளித்தார்' which is not stated in the article's wording but is a reasonable inference, so it is an invented detail: the article says the complaint was filed ('புகாரில்') but does not say the complaint was filed immediately after discovery.
  The caption's 'நடவடிக்கை' section and reel_script say the police are 'தேடி வருகின்றனர்' — consistent with the article; no problem there.
